{\rtf1\ansi\uc1{\*\generator WTS5;}\adeflang1025\adeff0\deff0\stshfdbch0\stshfloch0\stshfhich0\deflang1033\deflangfe1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1\fcharset0 Latha;}{\f2\fcharset0 Arial;}{\f3\fcharset0 MEPS Bookman WTS;}{\f4\fbidi\fcharset177 Arial;}}{\colortbl ;\red128\green0\blue128;\red0\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green128\blue0;\red153\green51\blue102;\red102\green102\blue153;\red51\green51\blue204;\red128\green0\blue0;}{\stylesheet {\s2\ltrpar\qc \rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\fs36\cf1\b \sbasedon0\snext21 Title;}{\s10\ltrpar\qc \rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\fs24\cf8\b \sbasedon0\snext25 Heading 1;}}\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033\ltrdoc\fcs1\af0\afs24\acf0\fcs0\f0\fs24\cf0{\info\uc1{\upr{\*\ud{\author \u67?\u111?\u112?\u121?\u114?\u105?\u103?\u104?\u116?\u32?\u169?\u32?\u50?\u48?\u50?\u49?\u32?\u87?\u97?\u116?\u99?\u104?\u32?\u84?\u111?\u119?\u101?\u114?\u32?\u66?\u105?\u98?\u108?\u101?\u32?\u97?\u110?\u100?\u32?\u84?\u114?\u97?\u99?\u116?\u32?\u83?\u111?\u99?\u105?\u101?\u116?\u121?\u32?\u111?\u102?\u32?\u80?\u101?\u110?\u110?\u115?\u121?\u108?\u118?\u97?\u110?\u105?\u97?}}}{\upr{\*\ud{\title \u76?\u101?\u115?\u115?\u111?\u110?\u160?\u49?\u52?\u8212?\u72?\u111?\u119?\u32?\u67?\u97?\u110?\u32?\u79?\u117?\u114?\u32?\u87?\u111?\u114?\u115?\u104?\u105?\u112?\u32?\u66?\u101?\u32?\u80?\u108?\u101?\u97?\u115?\u105?\u110?\u103?\u32?\u116?\u111?\u32?\u71?\u111?\u100?\u63?}}}}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\s2\qc {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\fs36\cf1\b Lesson\u160?14\u8212?How Can Our Worship Be Pleasing to God?\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 As discussed in the preceding lesson, not all religions please God. However, we }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\i can }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 worship our Creator in a way that makes him happy. What is \u8220?the form of worship [or, religion]\u8221? that pleases him? (}{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?pub=nwtsty&bible=59001027&wtlocale=E&srcid=share" }}{\fldrslt{\cs3\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2\ul James 1:27}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 , footnote) Consider what the Bible teaches.\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3 [Image:]\u160?A group of Jehovah\u8217?s Witnesses and visitors singing at a congregation meeting.\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b 1. On what should our worship be based?\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 Our worship should be based on the Bible. Jesus said to God: }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b \u8220?Your word is truth.\u8221? }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 (}{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?pub=nwtsty&bible=43017017&wtlocale=E&srcid=share" }}{\fldrslt{\cs3\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2\ul John 17:17}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 ) Some religions ignore the truth found in God\u8217?s inspired Word, the Bible. They replace it with human teachings and traditions. But Jehovah is not pleased with those who \u8220?disregard the commandment of God.\u8221? (Read Mark 7:9.) On the other hand, we bring joy to his heart when we stick to the Bible and follow its advice.\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3 [\u8220?Read\u8221? scripture] Mark 7:9: Further, he said to them: \u8220?You skillfully disregard the commandment of God in order to keep your tradition. [End of \u8220?Read\u8221? scripture]\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b 2. How should we worship Jehovah?\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 As our Creator, Jehovah deserves our exclusive devotion. (}{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?pub=nwtsty&bible=66004011&wtlocale=E&srcid=share" }}{\fldrslt{\cs3\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2\ul Revelation 4:11}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 ) This means that we must love him and worship only him, without the use of any idol, image, or icon.\u8212?Read Isaiah 42:8.\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3 [\u8220?Read\u8221? scripture] Isaiah 42:8: I am Jehovah. That is my name; I give my glory to no one else, Nor my praise to graven images. [End of \u8220?Read\u8221? scripture]\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 Our worship must be }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b \u8220?holy and acceptable\u8221? }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 to Jehovah. (}{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?pub=nwtsty&bible=45012001&wtlocale=E&srcid=share" }}{\fldrslt{\cs3\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2\ul Romans 12:1}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 ) This means that we need to live by his moral standards. For example, those who love Jehovah love and follow his standards for marriage. And they avoid harmful practices, such as the use of tobacco or the misuse of drugs or alcohol.\u160?*\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\cf3 [Footnote] }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\cf4 * These topics will be discussed in later lessons.}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f0\cf3  [End of footnote]\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b 3. Why should we worship Jehovah with fellow believers?\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 Our weekly meetings give us the opportunity to }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b \u8220?praise Jehovah .\u160?.\u160?. in the congregation.\u8221? }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 (}{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?pub=nwtsty&bible=19111001-19111002&wtlocale=E&srcid=share" }}{\fldrslt{\cs3\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2\ul Psalm 111:1,2}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 ) One way we do this is by singing praises to God. (Read Psalm 104:33.) Jehovah asks us to attend meetings because he loves us and he knows that they will help us to enjoy life forever. When we meet together for encouragement, we benefit ourselves.\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3 [\u8220?Read\u8221? scripture] Psalm 104:33: I will sing to Jehovah throughout my life; I will sing praises to my God as long as I live. [End of \u8220?Read\u8221? scripture]\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 \par\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\qc\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2 Dig Deeper\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 Examine why Jehovah does not approve of the use of images in worship. Learn important ways that we can praise God.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b 4. We should not use images in our worship\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 How do we know that doing so would be displeasing to God? Play the video, }{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?srcid=share&wtlocale=E&lank=pub-ebtv_503_VIDEO" }}{\fldrslt{\cs3\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2\i\ul Does God Approve the Use of Images in Worship}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ai\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\i ?}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2  (3:26) and then discuss the question that follows.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? What happened when some of God\u8217?s people in Bible times tried to worship him with the help of an idol?\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 Some people try to feel closer to God by using images in their worship. But could doing so actually push him away? }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b Read Exodus 20:4-6 and }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3\b Psalm 106:35, 3}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b 6,}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2  and then discuss these questions:\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? What objects or images have you seen people use in their worship?\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? How does Jehovah feel about the use of images?\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? How do you feel about using images?\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3 [\u8220?Read\u8221? scriptures] Exodus 20:4-6: \u8220?You must not make for yourself a carved image or a form like anything that is in the heavens above or on the earth below or in the waters under the earth. You must not bow down to them nor be enticed to serve them, for I, Jehovah your God, am a God who requires exclusive devotion, bringing punishment for the error of fathers upon sons, upon the third generation and upon the fourth generation of those who hate me, but showing loyal love to the thousandth generation of those who love me and keep my commandments.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3 Psalm 106:35, 36: But they mingled with the nations And adopted their ways. They kept serving their idols, And these became a snare to them. [End of \u8220?Read\u8221? scriptures]\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3 [Image:]\u160?Collage: 1.\u160?Israelites worship a statue of a golden calf a the foot of Mount Sinai. 2.\u160?A man holding a rosary prays in front of a statue of the virgin Mary.\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b 5. Worshipping only Jehovah liberates us from false ideas\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 See how worshipping Jehovah acceptably can liberate us from false ideas. Play the video }{\field{\*\fldinst {HYPERLINK "https://www.jw.org/finder?srcid=share&wtlocale=E&lank=pub-lffv_146_VIDEO" }}{\fldrslt{\cs3\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf2\i\ul Liberated by Truth}}}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2  (5:16).\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b Read Psalm 91:14,}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2  and then discuss this question:\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? What does Jehovah promise to do for us when we show that we love him by worshipping only him?\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3 [\u8220?Read\u8221? scripture] Psalm 91:14: God said: \u8220?Because he has affection for me, I will rescue him. I will protect him because he knows my name. [End of \u8220?Read\u8221? scripture]\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3\b 6}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b . We worship God at congregation meetings\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 We praise Jehovah and build each other up by singing and giving comments at congregation meetings. }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b Read Psalm 22:22, }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 and then discuss these questions:\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? Have you enjoyed hearing comments at the meetings?\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? Would you like to prepare to give a comment?\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3 [\u8220?Read\u8221? scripture] Psalm 22:22: I will declare your name to my brothers; In the midst of the congregation I will praise you. [End of \u8220?Read\u8221? scripture]\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3 [Image:]\u160?Collage: A female Bible student learning to worship God acceptably. 1.\u160?She sings praises to God at a congregation meeting. 2.\u160?She comments during a congregation meeting. 3.\u160?She shows a Bible-based video to a woman and her daughter.\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b 7. Jehovah is pleased when we share what we learn\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 There are many ways that we can share Bible truths with others. }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b Read Psalms 9:1 and 34:1, }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 and then discuss this question:\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? What is something you have learned from the Bible that you would like to tell someone else about?\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\li720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3 [\u8220?Read\u8221? scriptures] Psalm 9:1: I will praise you, O\u160?Jehovah, with all my heart; I will tell about all your wonderful works.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af2\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3 Psalm 34:1: I will praise Jehovah at all times; His praise will be on my lips constantly. [End of \u8220?Read\u8221? scriptures]\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 \par\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi720 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3 [Box] }{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf5 Some People Say: \u8220?It\u8217?s impossible to please God.\u8221?\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi-480\li480 \par{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf7 \u8226? What do you think?}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf3  [End of box]\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\s10\qc {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\cf8\b Summary\par}\pard\plain\langnp1033\langfenp1033 \ltrpar\ql\fi576 {\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 We please our Creator when we worship only him, praise him at congregation meetings, and share with others what we have learned.\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2\b Review\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? How can we learn how to worship God acceptably?\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1033\af1\ltrch\fcs0\lang1033\langnp1033\langfe1033\langfenp1033\f2 \u8226? Why should we worship only Jehovah?\par}{\rtlch\fcs1\alang1